# Python Backend Rules

## Structure
Feature-based organization: each feature is a directory under `app/` with:
- `router.py` — FastAPI route handlers (thin, delegate to service)
- `service.py` — Business logic
- `schemas.py` — Pydantic request/response models
- `repository.py` — Data access (when DB is added)
- `dependencies.py` — Feature-specific dependency injection

## Code Style
- Python 3.12+, use modern type hints (e.g., `list[str]` not `List[str]`)
- Format with `ruff format`, lint with `ruff check`
- Use `async def` for route handlers
- Pydantic v2 for all schemas
- No business logic in route handlers — delegate to service layer

## Testing
- Tests mirror app structure under `tests/`
- Use `TestClient` from FastAPI for API tests
- Run: `cd apps/api && source .venv/bin/activate && pytest -v`

## Dependencies
- Managed via `pyproject.toml` with `uv`
- Install: `cd apps/api && uv venv && source .venv/bin/activate && uv pip install -e ".[dev]"`
